====================================================================================================
2. g~ to PPN order; PPN parameters from g~_00 and from g~_0i independently
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] 2a g~_00 = -1 + 2 nu U and g~_ij = (1 + 2 nu U) delta_ij: the physical potential is U~ = nu U with nu = 1 + 1/mu_s, and gamma~ = 1 exactly
           (coeff(U) in g~_00 = 2 + 2/mu_s, in g~_ij = 2 + 2/mu_s)
  [PASS] 2b the U^2 term is -2 (nu U)^2 = -2 U~^2: beta~ = 1 at the level of the metric map (the nonlinear source correction is the TeVeS one, beta = 1)
           (coeff(U^2) = -2 - 4/mu_s - 2/mu_s**2)
    from g~_00:  alpha1~ = (alpha1_ae*mu_s - 8)/(mu_s + 1),   alpha2~ = alpha2_ae*mu_s/(mu_s + 1)
    from g~_0i:  alpha1~ = (alpha1_ae*mu_s - 8)/(mu_s + 1),   alpha2~ = alpha2_ae*mu_s/(mu_s + 1)
  [PASS] 2c the two independent extractions agree: alpha1~ = [alpha1_ae - 8 (nu - 1)]/nu,  alpha2~ = alpha2_ae/nu
  [PASS] 2d rest-frame route (V_i + W_i sum invariant): alpha1~ = (8 + alpha1_ae)/nu - 8, identical to the moving-frame value
  [PASS] 2e the Brans-Dicke control: with a CONFORMAL coupling only, gamma_BD = (2 - nu)/nu compensates the 1/nu gravitomagnetic deficit and alpha1 = 0
           (-(2 gamma + 2) = -4/nu: the disformal term forces gamma~ = 1 and moves the deficit into alpha1~)

