SW04 COMPLETE: 8/11 checks PASS.  VERDICT: the SW03 action FAILS the preferred-frame PPN bounds.  gamma~ = 1 and beta~ = 1 hold, but
alpha1~ = [alpha1_ae - 8(nu(eta_gal) - 1)]/nu(eta_gal) = -1.3 to -1.7 with a healthy aether, four orders above |alpha1| < 1e-4 (and the Nordtvedt
eta_N = -alpha1~ four orders above 4e-4).  THEOREM: a scalar that renormalises the Newtonian and light-bending potentials equally (gamma = 1,
forced by Cassini and by lensing) but contributes nothing to gravitomagnetism produces alpha1 = -8(nu - 1)/nu; an isotropic external-field
effect makes nu(eta_gal) - 1 = 0.19-0.26 uniform across the solar system; hence the isotropic-EFE + preferred-frame-lensing class is dead
on alpha1 exactly where the local-switch class is dead on the quadrupole.  Cancellation needs c14 < 0 (unstable aether) tuned to the Sun's eta.
